+# Password Hashing
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to hash passwords with argon2id. It was chosen for its memory-hard construction, which makes GPU- and ASIC-based brute-force attacks significantly more expensive than they are against low-memory algorithms. No further parameters (such as memory, iteration or parallelism settings) are recorded.
